From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: OMAP4: steelhead: write reboot reason to SAR scratchpad

The immutable stock OMAP4460 bootloader on the Google Nexus Q (steelhead)
enters fastboot or recovery on a warm reboot by reading a NUL-terminated
ASCII reason string from SAR RAM at offset 0xA0C.  SAR RAM is in the
always-on power domain and survives the PRM global warm SW reset issued by
omap_prm_reset_system(), so a string written there by Linux is still present
when u-boot runs on the next boot.

The stock 3.0.8 kernel populated this from a reboot notifier
(steelhead_reboot_notifier_handler): on SYS_RESTART it zeroed 0x20 bytes at
SAR+0xA0C, wrote the default "normal", then overrode it with "bootloader",
"recovery" or "recovery:wipe_data" according to the reboot command string.
Mainline never carried this -- omap44xx_restart() literally carries an
"XXX Should save 'cmd' into scratchpad" TODO and drops @cmd on the floor --
so "reboot bootloader" was ignored and the box could only be put into the
bootloader by physically pulling mains power (undesirable on an appliance
with an integrated mains SMPS and a single slow-blow fuse).

Implement the stock write, guarded to the steelhead machine, right where the
mainline TODO asked for it: just before the warm reset, in process context
via the machine .restart hook, touching only the already-mapped SAR RAM
(no allocation, safe with IRQs off).  The offset (0xA0C), the buffer clear
(0x20) and the four reason strings match the stock u-boot/kernel byte for
byte, so "systemctl reboot bootloader" over ssh now lands the device in
fastboot with no hands on the power cord.

Signed-off-by: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap4-restart.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap4-restart.c
@@ -5,9 +5,54 @@
 
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/reboot.h>
+#include <linux/io.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include "common.h"
 #include "prm.h"
 
+/*
+ * steelhead (Google Nexus Q) reboot-reason handoff to the stock u-boot.
+ *
+ * The immutable stock OMAP4460 bootloader decides whether to enter fastboot
+ * or recovery on a warm reboot by reading a NUL-terminated ASCII reason
+ * string from SAR RAM at offset 0xA0C.  SAR RAM lives in the always-on
+ * domain and survives the PRM global *warm* SW reset that
+ * omap_prm_reset_system() issues, so the string set here is still there when
+ * u-boot runs.  The stock 3.0.8 kernel wrote it from a reboot notifier
+ * (steelhead_reboot_notifier_handler); mainline dropped it -- this is the
+ * "XXX Should save 'cmd' into scratchpad" TODO below, implemented -- so
+ * "reboot bootloader" never reached fastboot and the box could only be put
+ * into the bootloader by pulling mains power.  Reproduce the stock write so
+ * it can be done over ssh with "systemctl reboot bootloader".  The strings
+ * ("normal" default, "bootloader", "recovery", "recovery:wipe_data") and the
+ * 0xA0C offset match the stock u-boot / kernel exactly.
+ */
+#define STEELHEAD_SAR_REBOOT_REASON	0xA0C
+
+static void steelhead_set_reboot_reason(const char *cmd)
+{
+	void __iomem *sar = omap4_get_sar_ram_base();
+	void __iomem *reason;
+	const char *s = "normal";
+
+	if (!sar)
+		return;
+	reason = sar + STEELHEAD_SAR_REBOOT_REASON;
+
+	/* Match stock: clear 0x20 bytes, default "normal", override by cmd. */
+	memset_io(reason, 0, 0x20);
+	if (cmd) {
+		if (!strcmp(cmd, "bootloader"))
+			s = "bootloader";
+		else if (!strcmp(cmd, "recovery"))
+			s = "recovery";
+		else if (!strcmp(cmd, "recovery:wipe_data"))
+			s = "recovery:wipe_data";
+	}
+	memcpy_toio(reason, s, strlen(s) + 1);
+}
+
 /**
  * omap44xx_restart - trigger a software restart of the SoC
  * @mode: the "reboot mode", see arch/arm/kernel/{setup,process}.c
@@ -18,6 +63,7 @@
  */
 void omap44xx_restart(enum reboot_mode mode, const char *cmd)
 {
-	/* XXX Should save 'cmd' into scratchpad for use after reboot */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("google,steelhead"))
+		steelhead_set_reboot_reason(cmd);
 	omap_prm_reset_system();
 }
